WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Some of the most important surfaces of a surgical instrument are also the hardest to see.

2
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:18.000
Sterile processing professionals inspect increasingly complex instruments. But seeing the image is only the beginning.

3
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:29.000
LumenAI brings image acquisition directly into the inspection workflow — capture from a compatible borescope or use an existing image without leaving the inspection.

4
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:36.000
The acquisition layer is designed around compatible image sources — not a single borescope manufacturer.

5
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:48.000
The image becomes structured evidence. LumenAI can support image assessment, surface visible findings, and compare with an approved baseline when one is available.

6
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:58.000
When uncertainty or defined review criteria are present, LumenAI routes the inspection for qualified human review. AI assists. People decide.

7
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:09.000
Each inspection can become part of a traceable record — connecting the instrument, image, baseline, findings, review history, and audit evidence over time.

8
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:20.000
LumenAI also creates a governed pathway for manufacturers, vendors, and healthcare organizations to contribute and use trusted reference information.

9
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:29.000
What begins with one inspection can become operational intelligence — patterns across instruments, departments, and time.

10
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:35.000
LumenAI. Inspection intelligence for Sterile Processing.
